    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0dd4aecc_d2b466ce",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-14T18:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Adding a property to list the versions is out of scope here, yes. However that wasn\u0027t the main point, it\u0027s rather about creating ninja rules for all versions instead of this variable.\n\nThe reason I brought it up here is that we\u0027re picking a direction on it with this CL. This approach is a bit ugly for the reason I explained initially, but it is perhaps the pragmatic one.",
      "parentUuid": "4d99556a_6a8d9dae",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1070a4fb_5824db4a",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T00:24:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suggest \"unversioned\" for this; it\u0027s more descriptive. Also, following on the subject above, we could consider a mode to disable the SDK snapshot generation altogether to save resources, and \"none\" would be better suited for that.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aa8f900d_333511d5",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060959
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T13:08:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this meant to be used to get modules that override their source equivalent? Meaning `java_sdk_library_import { name: \"framework-sdkextensions\" }` for example?\n\nIsn\u0027t that what current is? Do we need both? (maybe \"current\" should not have a -current suffix?)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c6253dd_9c4ba6ab",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T14:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see the distinction between ...VERSION\u003dnone and VERSION\u003dunversioned. They mean the same. Sure, \"unversioned\" has more meaning than \"none\" when not used in the context of the snapshot version but that does not happen here.\n\nAlso, using ...VERSION\u003dnone to disable snapshot generation altogether seems a little confusing. If required then an explicit environment variable, e.g. SOONG_SDK_SNAPSHOT_DISABLE\u003dtrue would be clearer.",
      "parentUuid": "1070a4fb_5824db4a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "68e85c3c_1eef60b3",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T14:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, they are unversioned modules.\n\n\"current\" (which is the default) creates versioned modules as well as unversioned modules. A versioned module has names of the format \"\u003csdk\u003e_\u003cmodule\u003e@\u003cversion\u003e\". So, \"current\" will create modules called \"\u003csdk\u003e_\u003cmodule\u003e@current\".\n\nAt the moment the \"current\" modules aren\u0027t actually used, although they do help detect and prevent build changes that would break versioned modules.",
      "parentUuid": "aa8f900d_333511d5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f900196d_e3841bba",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-10T15:21:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The plan in go/android-module-sdk is to set uses_sdks in apex{} modules to pick the SDK to use, and then with \"current\" we\u0027d use the @current modules rather than the unversioned ones, and at that point we wouldn\u0027t need the latter anymore.\n\n(We wouldn\u0027t be able to use the \"prefer\" flag to flip between source and @current prebuilts then either, so USE_ANDROID_MODULE_PREBUILTS in go/module-sdk-prefer-prebuilts would need to control the source vs @current selection.)",
      "parentUuid": "68e85c3c_1eef60b3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b3c7eeae_17e89cec",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-10T15:21:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"none\" only works in the context of this variable, elsewhere it\u0027s more ambiguous and \"unversioned\" is preferable. I think it\u0027s better to use \"unversioned\" everywhere for consistency.\n\nAs for disabling the snapshots altogether, I think that if we go for this environment variable, then disabled should be the default if it isn\u0027t set. When there are different kinds of snapshots that can be produced and we have to pick one, it makes sense to have to always specify it explicitly.",
      "parentUuid": "3c6253dd_9c4ba6ab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4b0837f6_423615b0",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-12T21:20:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Changed to \"unversioned\".\n\nDisabling the generation of the snapshot unless this variable is set will break a lot of existing behavior from Soong unit tests to build scripts. That would involve a lot of work that is not justified for the goals of this change.",
      "parentUuid": "b3c7eeae_17e89cec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5896b95_d22989e9",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-12T21:20:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The unversioned ones would still be needed for those dependencies that are not part of an APEX or if the APEX does not set the version. I can\u0027t see anything in that document that requires the APEX to use @current. There are some comments that indicate it may not be a good idea.",
      "parentUuid": "f900196d_e3841bba",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dc41a760_e11807d7",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-14T18:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fixing the Soong tests is just a matter of adding a preparer, isn\u0027t it? I think there are two or three build scripts that would need patching, so I wouldn\u0027t say it\u0027s \"a lot of work\". But I can agree it\u0027s out of scope here.",
      "parentUuid": "4b0837f6_423615b0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e55e2da4_49e17138",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 14,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-14T18:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The unversioned ones would still be needed for those dependencies that are not part of an APEX\n\nYou mean platform dependencies? If so, I think for the purposes of this system it\u0027s more consistent and easier to treat platform as another APEX, i.e. use uses_sdks there too to control its dependencies on APEXes.\n\n\u003e I can\u0027t see anything in that document that requires the APEX to use @current.\n\nThe question is rather if there\u0027s a reason to _not_ control it through uses_libs and @current - we\u0027ll need that method and should avoid another method if we can.\n\n\u003e There are some comments that indicate it may not be a good idea.\n\nThat\u0027s interesting. There are a lot of comments on that doc; can you link to the ones you\u0027re referring to?",
      "parentUuid": "c5896b95_d22989e9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 14,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 14,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2380f734_3677ebfe",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060959
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T13:08:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we have any way to know what the last frozen sdk snapshot is? For the non-module SDK, we have the prebuilt_sdk module type which looks at all the versions and creates some meta modules like foo-last-frozen based on the contents of the dirs.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c70ac53_28a1858f",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 18,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-07T14:28:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not yet. Given that we don\u0027t actually have any modules that have been versioned (other then the unused @current) we haven\u0027t needed it. That is a hole that definitely needs fixing.",
      "parentUuid": "2380f734_3677ebfe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 18,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 18,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "defd345f0ebda7b433fd0b8d59a5ac0d0493c5d8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
